    summary: "A head-to-head comparison of IELTS Academic, PTE Academic, and TOEFL iBT across exam fees in Bangladesh, score turnaround times, speaking test format, and university acceptance.",
    content: "## Introduction\n\nA head-to-head comparison of IELTS Academic, PTE Academic, and TOEFL iBT across exam fees in Bangladesh, score turnaround times, speaking test format, and university acceptance.\n\nNavigating international admissions, degree comparisons, and student visas requires a rigorous understanding of institutional criteria rather than relying on commercial marketing. This guide provides an evidence-based breakdown designed specifically for prospective international applicants.\n\n## Transparent Comparison Matrix\n\nThe following table outlines key verified criteria across evaluated institutions and regulatory policies. Data is sourced from official university publications, regulatory statutes, and national accreditation registries.\n\n\n| Feature | IELTS Academic | PTE Academic | TOEFL iBT |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Test Duration | 2 hours 45 minutes | 2 hours | Approximately 2 hours |\n| Speaking Evaluation | In-person 1-on-1 human interview (11–14 mins) | Automated computer mic recording, scored entirely by AI | Computer mic recording, scored by combination of AI and certified human raters |\n| Official BD Cost (2026) | BDT 26,500 | $215 USD (~BDT 26,230) | $205 USD (~BDT 25,000) |\n| Result Turnaround | 3–5 days (computer), 13 days (paper) | 1–2 business days (typically under 48 hours) | 4–8 business days |\n| Global University Acceptance | Universal across UK, AU, CA, NZ, IE; widely accepted in US and Europe | Widely accepted in UK, AU, NZ, IE; expanding in US and Canada | Universal across US and Canada; widely accepted across UK and Europe |\n| Home-Edition Visa Risk | IELTS Indicator / Online barred by UKVI and IRCC for visas | PTE Online explicitly barred by UKVI and Australian Home Affairs | TOEFL Home Edition barred by UKVI; rejected by Oxford and top faculties |\n\n## The Trinity of Standardized English Testing\n\nWhen evaluating the trinity of standardized english testing, international students must adhere to published institutional guidelines rather than assumptions. Admissions committees and visa caseworkers review student dossiers against strict statutory benchmarks.\n\n### Key Evaluation Considerations\n- **Official Verification**: Always consult primary university catalog handbooks and government portals.\n- **Sub-Band Criteria**: Meeting an overall threshold does not compensate for deficient prerequisite subject scores.\n- **Document Integrity**: Transcripts and financial evidence must undergo verifiable institutional attestation.\n\n## Human Interviewer (IELTS) vs. AI Microphone Speaking (PTE & TOEFL)\n\nWhen evaluating human interviewer (ielts) vs. ai microphone speaking (pte & toefl), international students must adhere to published institutional guidelines rather than assumptions. Admissions committees and visa caseworkers review student dossiers against strict statutory benchmarks.\n\n### Key Evaluation Considerations\n- **Official Verification**: Always consult primary university catalog handbooks and government portals.\n- **Sub-Band Criteria**: Meeting an overall threshold does not compensate for deficient prerequisite subject scores.\n- **Document Integrity**: Transcripts and financial evidence must undergo verifiable institutional attestation.\n\n## Score Turnaround Time: Planning for Urgent Deadlines\n\nWhen evaluating score turnaround time: planning for urgent deadlines, international students must adhere to published institutional guidelines rather than assumptions. Admissions committees and visa caseworkers review student dossiers against strict statutory benchmarks.\n\n### Key Evaluation Considerations\n- **Official Verification**: Always consult primary university catalog handbooks and government portals.\n- **Sub-Band Criteria**: Meeting an overall threshold does not compensate for deficient prerequisite subject scores.\n- **Document Integrity**: Transcripts and financial evidence must undergo verifiable institutional attestation.\n\n## Fee Comparison in Bangladesh: BDT 26,500 (IELTS) vs. $215 (PTE) vs. $205 (TOEFL)\n\nWhen evaluating fee comparison in bangladesh: bdt 26,500 (ielts) vs. $215 (pte) vs. $205 (toefl), international students must adhere to published institutional guidelines rather than assumptions. Admissions committees and visa caseworkers review student dossiers against strict statutory benchmarks.\n\n### Key Evaluation Considerations\n- **Official Verification**: Always consult primary university catalog handbooks and government portals.\n- **Sub-Band Criteria**: Meeting an overall threshold does not compensate for deficient prerequisite subject scores.\n- **Document Integrity**: Transcripts and financial evidence must undergo verifiable institutional attestation.\n\n## Three-Way Direct Test Comparison Table\n\nWhen evaluating three-way direct test comparison table, international students must adhere to published institutional guidelines rather than assumptions. Admissions committees and visa caseworkers review student dossiers against strict statutory benchmarks.\n\n### Key Evaluation Considerations\n- **Official Verification**: Always consult primary university catalog handbooks and government portals.\n- **Sub-Band Criteria**: Meeting an overall threshold does not compensate for deficient prerequisite subject scores.\n- **Document Integrity**: Transcripts and financial evidence must undergo verifiable institutional attestation.\n\n## Which Test Suits Your Personal Test-Taking Strengths?\n\nWhen evaluating which test suits your personal test-taking strengths?, international students must adhere to published institutional guidelines rather than assumptions. Admissions committees and visa caseworkers review student dossiers against strict statutory benchmarks.\n\n### Key Evaluation Considerations\n- **Official Verification**: Always consult primary university catalog handbooks and government portals.\n- **Sub-Band Criteria**: Meeting an overall threshold does not compensate for deficient prerequisite subject scores.\n- **Document Integrity**: Transcripts and financial evidence must undergo verifiable institutional attestation.\n\n## Important Limitations and Eligibility Caveats\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> Academic policies, visa regulations, and tuition fees are subject to periodic regulatory updates. Meeting minimum published requirements does not guarantee admission or student visa issuance. Always cross-verify with official university course pages and destination country diplomatic consular instructions.\n\n## Next Steps for Prospective Students\n\n1. Audit your secondary and undergraduate transcripts against published prerequisite subjects.\n2. Verify the exact English language requirements for your specific course and target degree level.\n3. Prepare your official financial sponsorship and banking evidence according to statutory holding rules.\n4. Use the Borno Higher Study [Eligibility Checker](/eligibility-checker) and [Tuition Calculator](/calculator) to assess your profile.",
